# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem
/.codex/

# image lab job log (cost metering, runtime data)
/var/

# Event promo material. Licensed stock photography, client-supplied portraits
# of real people, and supplied music stay out of the repository: pushing them
# would publish licensed and personal media into git history, which cannot be
# undone by a later delete. Partner logos (logos/) ARE committed — they are
# small, and the client cleared their use for this project.
#
# Regenerate from the material drop folder before rendering:
#   node labs/event/scripts/prepare-assets.mjs --src <dir> --slug <slug>
# Note that sake-2026's brief names these files, so a clone must run the script
# (or null the slots) before `npm run event:render` — Remotion fails a render on
# a missing image rather than silently dropping it, which is the behaviour we
# want: a slot is only "empty by design" when the brief says null.
/public/event/*/photos/
/public/event/*/art/
/public/event/*/bgm.mp3

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# python (blender scripts)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Default asset pool (lib/assets/defaults.ts). Two halves with OPPOSITE rules —
# docs/demo-assets.md §2 is the canonical statement of which is which.
#
# GITIGNORED, because the bytes may not be redistributed. The committed catalog
# entry naming them is what tells a fresh checkout what is missing.
#
# NOTE: the reason recorded here for bgm/ was corrected on 2026-08-15 and is no
# longer "unlicensed placeholders" — both tracks were generated with Suno AI on
# a commercial plan and ARE ours to publish (lib/assets/defaults.ts). So the
# bytes COULD be committed like the generated images below; whether to move them
# is an open decision, not a licensing constraint. Do not restore the old
# comment: it kept them out of every export for the wrong reason.
/public/defaults/bgm/*.mp3
# 効果音ラボ forbids redistributing the files themselves, so these genuinely
# cannot be committed. scripts/fetch-default-sfx.mjs restores them anywhere and
# the committed catalog.json records what belongs here.
/public/defaults/sfx/*.mp3
#
# COMMITTED, deliberately: public/defaults/{stills,portraits,marks,devices}/.
# Generated with Midjourney on a commercial plan (or authored as code), so they
# are ours to redistribute — the whole point of replacing the licensed stock and
# the real people's portraits under public/event/. They are NOT listed here.
# A generation recipe cannot restore them (the same prompt yields a different
# picture), so the repository has to hold the bytes rather than the recipe.
